# Type Safety: no `any`, no type-cast escapes

This repository requires strict, explicit typing.

## Rules

- Do not introduce `any` in new or modified code.
  - Forbidden: `: any`, `Array<any>`, `Record<string, any>`, `any[]`, generic defaults to `any`.
- Do not use type-cast escapes to silence type errors.
  - Forbidden: `as any`, `as unknown as T`, `<any>value`, broad unsafe assertions.
- Prefer proper typing at the source:
  - Add/adjust interfaces or union types.
  - Narrow unknown values with runtime guards.
  - Refactor code to keep type inference accurate instead of forcing assertions.

## Allowed exceptions

- Existing legacy code may remain untouched unless the task requires modifying it.
- Third-party/global bridge points (for example framework polyfills) may keep existing casts only when no typed alternative exists; do not expand this pattern.

## Agent checklist

1. When fixing type errors, first improve the type model, not assertions.
2. Before finishing, search changed files for `any` and `as ` assertions and remove unsafe ones.
3. If an assertion is truly unavoidable, document why in code comments and keep the narrowest possible type.
